					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3021428#post-3426648</guid>
				<title>Author Post</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3021428/the-long-goodbye#post-3426648</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 20 Jul 2017 08:13:43 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>3122708</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The sequel to <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/hartliss-detective-agency">Hartliss Detective Agency</a>! Warning: <em>STILL SUPER GROSS.</em></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Credit</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>If I forget you, please poke me and I'll update!</p> <ul> <li>Modern_Erasmus</li> <li>Pedantique</li> <li>Avocadonut</li> <li>AidenEldritch</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p>I linked a couple of the SCPs referenced here, but some of them I didn't &#8212; mostly 'cuz I thought it might be fun for some people to try and figure out what's being referenced. They're all series 1 stuff &#8212; I'll explain the references in spoilers below (but they're not crucial for the plot):</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SCP&nbsp;references</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <ul> <li>Part 1 is obviously <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-000">SCP-000</a>; dude just wants a friend :(</li> <li>Part 2 is <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-002">SCP-002</a>. Chicago's never looked nicer!</li> <li>Part 3 is, in order&#8230;</li> </ul> <blockquote> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-003">SCP-003</a> &#8212; looks like they had a breach, and a fly beat 'em to it D:</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-004">SCP-004</a> &#8212; It's bigger on the inside. D:</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-005">SCP-005</a> &#8212; Every door, everywhere, unlocking all at once. Including all of the Foundation's. D: D: D:</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-006">SCP-006</a> &#8212; IMMORTALITY SUCKS.</li> </ul> </blockquote> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-352">SCP-352</a>!</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-555">SCP-555</a> is having a corpse party and everyone's invited!</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-610">SCP-610</a> might not be Sarkic, but man oh man do the Sarkics wish they'd thought of it.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-701">SCP-701</a> says 'Eat your heart out, Orson Welles!'</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-871">SCP-871</a> can be blamed wholly on AidenEldritch, who suggested it. I guess we should have listened to Marie Antoinette. Lady knew what was up.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Also, if you missed it: There's hidden text in the first opening part (s'not crucial to the plot, though; just a cute extra!). Highlight or check the page source to see it! <hr /> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
